From: Zizheng Guo <gzz_2000@126.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tgsi: bound the vertices that the sanity check declares

tgsi_sanity_check declares each vertex of a tessellation control shader's
outputs, of as many vertices as the shader's TCS_VERTICES_OUT, which a
virgl guest's shader may have of 2^31: tgsi_text_translate, which checks
what it translates, allocated as many registers, for minutes. A patch has
32 vertices at most.

SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
---

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/tgsi_sanity.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/tgsi_sanity.c
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/tgsi_sanity.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/tgsi/tgsi_sanity.c
@@ -491,9 +491,12 @@
        prop->Property.PropertyName == TGSI_PROPERTY_GS_INPUT_PRIM) {
       ctx->implied_array_size = mesa_vertices_per_prim(prop->u[0].Data);
    }
+   /* The declarations of the outputs declare each vertex of the patch,
+    * which has 32 at most.
+    */
    if (iter->processor.Processor == MESA_SHADER_TESS_CTRL &&
        prop->Property.PropertyName == TGSI_PROPERTY_TCS_VERTICES_OUT)
-      ctx->implied_out_array_size = prop->u[0].Data;
+      ctx->implied_out_array_size = MIN2(prop->u[0].Data, 32);
    return true;
 }
 
